  "system": {
    "description": "",
    "tier": 1,
    "difficulty": 14,
    "potentialAdversaries": {},
    "notes": "<p><strong>Environment: Rush-Hour Elevated Highway</strong></p><p>A dense flow of commuters fills the multilane highway. Autonomous cars hold tight formation while human drivers weave unpredictably. Traffic speed oscillates between smooth motion and abrupt gridlock as routing algorithms struggle with peak load. Police speed traps sit on overpasses and median cutouts. Farther ahead, robotic construction rigs crawl along active repair zones, narrowing lanes and throwing sensor noise into the air.</p><p><strong>Complicating Features</strong></p><p><strong>Sudden Traffic Compression</strong><br />Routing shifts or lane merges can collapse flow instantly, forcing hard braking or rapid lane changes.</p><p><strong>Police Speed Traps</strong><br />High-resolution lidar and drone patrols sweep for velocity spikes and unusual maneuvering.</p><p><strong>Human Driver Variability</strong><br />Commuters make late merges, emergency stops, or erratic lane shifts that disrupt predictable movement.</p><p><strong>Autonomous Platoons</strong><br />Tightly grouped auto-cars leave little physical space; breaking into a platoon requires precision or force.</p><p><strong>Construction Rigs</strong><br />Large robotic equipment drifts across marked boundaries, shedding debris and throwing off targeting or sensor locks.</p><p><strong>Sensor Interference</strong><br />High signal density from vehicles, signage, and enforcement systems can degrade comms or targeting feeds.</p><p>This setup supports a high-velocity chase with constant positional constraints and external pressure from civilian and enforcement systems.</p>",
    "impulses": "",
    "type": "event",
    "attribution": {}
  },
